<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>FDOx to CIDOC CRM crosswalk</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink: #1c1c1c; --muted: #5c5c5c; --rule: #d8d4cc; --bg: #fbfaf7;
          --accent: #7a4b17; --warn: #8a1c1c; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 2rem 1.5rem 5rem; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
         font: 16px/1.55 "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif; }
  main { max-width: 62rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2.6rem 0 .4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
       padding-bottom: .3rem; }
  p { max-width: 46rem; }
  .lede { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: .8rem 0 0;
          font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: .84rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: .42rem .6rem;
           border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase;
       letter-spacing: .04em; font-size: .7rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  code, .term { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
                font-size: .82em; }
  .term { color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; }
  td.note { color: var(--muted); }
  .rule { white-space: nowrap; color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; }
  .count { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .warn { color: var(--warn); }
  .none td.target { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<h1>FDOx to CIDOC CRM crosswalk</h1>
<p class="lede">How the FDOx registry anchors harvested FDO metadata in CIDOC CRM,
following the <a href="https://nfdi4objects.github.io/crm-rdf-ap/">NFDI4Objects
CIDOC-CRM in RDF application profile</a>. Generated from
<code>crosswalks/fdo--crm.csv</code>; edit the table, not this page.</p>

<p>A row is one of five kinds. <strong>axiom</strong> states something about a
term in the FDOx or registry namespace and goes into
<code>metadata/crm_bridge.ttl</code>. <strong>ext-axiom</strong> quotes a
statement from an external ontology verbatim and names its source; nothing in
this repository is invented about a namespace it does not own.
<strong>normalise</strong> repairs an abbreviated class IRI that the generator
writes and that resolves to nothing. <strong>instance</strong> is materialised
per object when the bundle is built, because its subject is in a foreign
namespace. <strong>none</strong> is a term left deliberately unanchored, with
the reason beside it.</p>

{% for mechanism, rows in groups %}{% if rows %}
<h2>{{ mechanism }} <span class="meta">&mdash; {{ rows | length }} row{{ '' if rows | length == 1 else 's' }}</span></h2>
<table class="{{ mechanism }}">
<thead><tr>
  <th>Term</th><th>Kind</th><th>Target</th><th>Profile / source</th><th>Note</th>
</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for row in rows %}
<tr>
  <td class="term">{{ row.fdo_term }}</td>
  <td>{{ row.kind }}</td>
  <td class="target term">{{ row.target or '&mdash;' | safe }}</td>
  <td class="rule">{{ row.source or row.ap_rule }}</td>
  <td class="note">{{ row.note }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}

<h2>Role vocabulary</h2>
<p>The values <code>fdo:role</code> takes on a distribution, as SKOS concepts in
<code>{{ role_scheme }}</code>. The list is flat: the packages draw no hierarchy
between the values, and inventing one would put structure into the registry that
its sources do not carry. Counts are occurrences in the harvested packages the
registry can read.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Label</th><th>Definition</th><th class="count">In corpus</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for role in roles %}
<tr>
  <td class="term">{{ role.value }}</td>
  <td>{{ role.pref_label }}</td>
  <td class="note">{{ role.definition }}</td>
  <td class="count">{{ role.count }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>

{% if unreadable %}
<h2>Packages the registry cannot read</h2>
<p>The registry reads, it does not correct. A harvested
<code>fdo-metadata.ttl</code> that is not valid Turtle is skipped with a reason
and reported here and in the quality report; the fix belongs in the generator
that wrote it, not in the registry that reads it.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for record, reason in unreadable %}
<tr><td class="term warn">{{ record }}</td><td class="note">{{ reason }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}

<p class="meta" style="margin-top:3rem">FDOx Registry &middot; release {{ release }}
&middot; <a href="https://github.com/Research-Squirrel-Engineers/fdo-squirrel-registry">source</a></p>

</main>
</body>
</html>
